{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Braiding.HnMarkovTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Braiding.HnMarkovTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.markovTraceTower_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.markovTraceTower_canonical","kind":"instance","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/HnMarkovTrace.lean#L68-L111","doc":"Canonical concrete instance of `MarkovTraceTower q` for `q > 1`\n    (Wenzl positivity regime).\n\nThe instance uses:\n  - z = 1/(q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2})  (canonical Wenzl Markov parameter)\n  - trM_sigma1_sq n = (q^{5/2} − q^{1/2} + q² + q) / (q² + q) for all n\n    (Markov-invariant closed form proved in\n    `prop:trm-hopf-sigma1-sq-closed-form`)\n  - stabilises proof: the function is constant in n, so trivially equal.\n\nThe numerical implementation lives in\n`computations/markov_peel.tr_M_atomic` (Python; uses\nGS reduction + Markov-axiom recursive ascent). The Lean class\ninstance here mirrors that semantic at the type level.\n\n**Convention D** (owner ruling R1, 2026-08-15), migrated from convention C\n2026-08-26 (bean `qou-cxjq`). This instance previously set\n`z := 1/(√q + 1/√q)` — convention C — and was the single most load-bearing\nconvention site in the tree: it is the tower downstream Jones-value code resolves\nagainst. It was invisible to `scripts/lean-markov-convention-audit.py` until that\nscanner learned to read `instance` field assignments, because a convention set by\na *field* is not set by a `def` body (detector-blindness taxonomy #15).\n\nBoth fields move together, and they have to. `trM_sigma1_sq` is the Markov trace\nof the Hopf braid `σ₁²`, which the Markov axiom fixes as `h·z + 1`; the committed\nconvention-C value `(q^{5/2} − q^{1/2} + q² + q)/(q² + q)` is exactly that at\n`z = z_C` (verified symbolically). Migrating `z` alone would have left the\ninstance internally inconsistent — a tower whose `z` and whose Hopf trace came\nfrom different conventions.\n\nUnder convention D the same identity gives\n`h·z_D + 1 = (q − q⁻¹)·q³/(q²+1) + 1 = (q⁴ + 1)/(q² + 1)`,\nwhich is **fully rational in `q`**. So the note that used to sit here — that\nreal-valued `q^{1/2}` requires `Real.sqrt`, used via `Real.sqrt_pos` for the\npositivity proof — no longer applies: convention D removes every square root\nfrom this instance, positivity included. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceTower.trM_sigma1_sq_stabilises","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceTower.trM_sigma1_sq_stabilises","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/HnMarkovTrace.lean#L64-L64","doc":"Markov-invariance: for every n ≥ 2, the trace of σ_1² is the\nsame as in H_2 (since σ_1² involves only the first generator,\nextra strands stabilise trivially: z · z⁻¹ = 1).\n\nThis is property (M3)' applied to σ_1² ∈ H_2 ⊆ H_n. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceTower.trM_sigma1_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceTower.trM_sigma1_sq","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/HnMarkovTrace.lean#L58-L58","doc":"The Markov trace at H_n: σ_1² → ℝ. This abstracts over the\nconcrete Hecke-algebra elements; only the trace of the Hopf\nbraid σ_1² in H_n is needed here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceTower.z_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceTower.z_pos","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/HnMarkovTrace.lean#L54-L54","doc":"z is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceTower.z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceTower.z","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/HnMarkovTrace.lean#L52-L52","doc":"The Markov parameter. **The class does not fix a convention** — an\ninstance does, by what it assigns here. This docstring used to read\n`z = 1/(q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2})`, i.e. it named convention C at the *class*\nlevel, which is the wrong place for it: the class is the abstraction over\ntowers, and a convention is a property of an instance. Corrected 2026-08-26\n(bean `qou-cxjq`). The canonical instance below is convention D. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceTower.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceTower.mk","kind":"ctor","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/HnMarkovTrace.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceTower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceTower","kind":"class","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/HnMarkovTrace.lean#L27-L66","doc":"Canonical Markov-trace tower abstraction.\n\n`MarkovTraceTower q` parameterises a family of trace maps\n`tr_n : H_n(q) → ℝ` (one per n ≥ 1) satisfying the three Markov-trace\naxioms (Jones 1987 §2):\n\n  (M1) Normalisation:    tr_n(1) = 1\n  (M2) Trace property:   tr_n(a · b) = tr_n(b · a)\n  (M3) Markov property:  tr_{n+1}(β · σ_n^{±1}) = z^{±1} · tr_n(β)\n                         for β ∈ H_n(q) and σ_n the new generator,\n                         with z := 1/(q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2}).\n\nFor abstract reasoning about cross-n invariance, the relevant\nproperty is (M3)' a STRENGTHENING of (M3): when σ_n is disjoint from\nβ (which is the case when β uses only generators σ_1..σ_{m-1} for\nm < n), the new strand contributes z · z⁻¹ = 1 in the stabilisation\nchain. Thus tr_n(β) = tr_m(β) for the canonical inclusion\nH_m ⊆ H_n. ","signatureChunk":0}]}